  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Evaluation Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an employee evaluation form?\", \"a\": \"It is the document a manager uses to rate how an employee performed over a review period. Most versions list the role's competencies with a rating scale, a comments box for each, a section on goals, and signature lines for both people.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to make an employee evaluation form?\", \"a\": \"Pick the review cycle and five to seven competencies for the role, then write a one-line definition for each rating. Require a comment on the lowest scores and add goals and signature lines. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> builds that form from a plain description of your cycle.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a filled-in evaluation form sample look like?\", \"a\": \"It names behavior and results. Closing 41 support tickets a week against a target of 35, with two escalations all quarter, says far more than calling someone a great worker. Any evaluation form sample worth copying pairs each rating with evidence like that and sets a measurable goal.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to fill an employee performance evaluation form?\", \"a\": \"Gather the employee's goals, any notes from the period, and their self-review before you open it. Rate one competency at a time against the scale's definitions. Write the example first and pick the score second. Leave the overall rating until every section of the performance evaluation form is done.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you write constructive criticism on a staff evaluation form?\", \"a\": \"Name the problem and the fix in the same comment. Example: three of five client reports this quarter went out late, and two needed corrections. Through June, drafts go to the manager two days before each deadline. On a staff evaluation form, criticism without a next step reads as a verdict.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should not be included in a personnel evaluation form?\", \"a\": \"Anything tied to a protected trait. Federal law bars treating employees differently because of age 40 or over, pregnancy, disability, religion, or national origin, among other traits. Leave out guesses about motives and comparisons with named coworkers. A personnel evaluation form should describe the work, not the person.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should a peer evaluation form ask?\", \"a\": \"Ask only about work a colleague has seen firsthand, such as how the person hands off tasks or handles disagreement. Five or six questions are enough, each with a rating and a required example. Every peer can answer in an app built with Emergent, with no per-seat pricing to cover. Feedback on managers works better through an anonymous feedback form.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I write on an employee self evaluation form?\", \"a\": \"Lead with results you can count against last cycle's goals, such as targets hit or projects shipped. Rate yourself honestly and give one example per rating. On an employee self evaluation form, name the skill you want to build next. If a course helped, say so in a training feedback form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide a template for an employee evaluation form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Open with a header for the employee, job title, reviewer, and review period. Below it, list each competency with its scale definitions and a comment box. Mark last cycle's goals met or missed, set new ones, and end with dated signature lines. Emergent can turn that outline into a working form from a one-paragraph description.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a performance review form the same as an employee evaluation form?\", \"a\": \"Mostly, yes. HR teams use the two names for the same document: ratings against the role's competencies, comments, and goals. When a company does split them, the performance review form covers the formal annual cycle, while evaluation forms also handle 90-day probation checks and project wrap-ups.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
